<div class="seed-instructions">

    <div class="seed-instructions-header">

        <div class="seed-instructions-icon">
            <i class="fa fa-seedling"></i>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h1>Seed Instructions</h1>
            <p>
                Help grow meaningful conversations and preserve
                knowledge across the Wahenga community.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>


    <div class="seed-instructions-content">

        {# ----------------------------------------------------------
           WHAT IS A SEED?
        ----------------------------------------------------------- #}

        <section class="seed-instruction-section">

            <div class="seed-section-heading">
                <span class="seed-section-icon">
                    <i class="fa fa-leaf"></i>
                </span>

                <div>
                    <h2>What is a Seed?</h2>
                    <p>Your role in the community</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="seed-instruction-card">

                <p>
                    A Seed is a community participant whose role is to
                    help conversations grow, encourage participation,
                    and help preserve useful knowledge.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Seeds are given specific tasks based on what is
                    happening in the community. Your task may involve
                    starting a conversation, answering a question,
                    sharing knowledge, or encouraging someone to
                    continue a discussion.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


        {# ----------------------------------------------------------
           HOW TASKS WORK
        ----------------------------------------------------------- #}

        <section class="seed-instruction-section">

            <div class="seed-section-heading">

                <span class="seed-section-icon">
                    <i class="fa fa-tasks"></i>
                </span>

                <div>
                    <h2>How Seed Tasks Work</h2>
                    <p>Follow the task workflow</p>
                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="seed-workflow">

                <div class="seed-workflow-step">

                    <div class="seed-step-number">1</div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Receive a Task</h3>

                        <p>
                            When an opportunity is identified, a task
                            may be assigned to you.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-workflow-step">

                    <div class="seed-step-number">2</div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Start the Task</h3>

                        <p>
                            Open the task and review the conversation
                            or activity you have been asked to engage with.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            When you are ready to work on it, select
                            <strong>Start this task</strong>.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-workflow-step">

                    <div class="seed-step-number">3</div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Complete the Task</h3>

                        <p>
                            Carry out the requested action naturally.
                            When you have finished, return to the task
                            and select <strong>Complete this task</strong>.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-workflow-step">

                    <div class="seed-step-number">4</div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Task Performance is Measured</h3>

                        <p>
                            Completed tasks may be measured against
                            community engagement and other relevant
                            objectives.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        {# ----------------------------------------------------------
           TASK STATUS
        ----------------------------------------------------------- #}

        <section class="seed-instruction-section">

            <div class="seed-section-heading">

                <span class="seed-section-icon">
                    <i class="fa fa-exchange-alt"></i>
                </span>

                <div>
                    <h2>Task Status</h2>
                    <p>What each status means</p>
                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="seed-status-list">

                <div class="seed-status-item">

                    <span class="seed-status-badge pending">
                        Pending
                    </span>

                    <p>
                        The task is available but has not yet been started.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-status-item">

                    <span class="seed-status-badge assigned">
                        Assigned
                    </span>

                    <p>
                        The task has been assigned to a Seed.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-status-item">

                    <span class="seed-status-badge progress">
                        In Progress
                    </span>

                    <p>
                        You have started working on the task.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-status-item">

                    <span class="seed-status-badge completed">
                        Completed
                    </span>

                    <p>
                        The task has been completed and can be
                        evaluated for performance.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-status-item">

                    <span class="seed-status-badge failed">
                        Failed
                    </span>

                    <p>
                        The task could not be completed successfully
                        and may be eligible for another attempt.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        {# ----------------------------------------------------------
           GOOD SEED BEHAVIOUR
        ----------------------------------------------------------- #}

        <section class="seed-instruction-section">

            <div class="seed-section-heading">

                <span class="seed-section-icon">
                    <i class="fa fa-heart"></i>
                </span>

                <div>
                    <h2>Being a Good Seed</h2>
                    <p>Quality matters more than activity</p>
                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="seed-guidelines">

                <div class="seed-guideline">

                    <i class="fa fa-comments"></i>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Be natural</strong>

                        <p>
                            Participate as a genuine member of the
                            community. Avoid making conversations feel
                            artificial or forced.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-guideline">

                    <i class="fa fa-question-circle"></i>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Be helpful</strong>

                        <p>
                            When responding to questions, provide useful
                            information and encourage further discussion.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-guideline">

                    <i class="fa fa-book"></i>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Preserve knowledge</strong>

                        <p>
                            When discussing heritage, family history,
                            traditions or culture, help bring useful
                            knowledge into the conversation.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-guideline">

                    <i class="fa fa-users"></i>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Encourage others</strong>

                        <p>
                            A good contribution should make it easier
                            for other community members to participate.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="seed-guideline">

                    <i class="fa fa-check-circle"></i>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Complete your tasks</strong>

                        <p>
                            Start tasks when you are ready to work on them
                            and mark them complete when the work is actually
                            finished.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        {# ----------------------------------------------------------
           IMPORTANT
        ----------------------------------------------------------- #}

        <section class="seed-instruction-note">

            <div class="seed-note-icon">
                <i class="fa fa-lightbulb"></i>
            </div>

            <div>

                <strong>Remember</strong>

                <p>
                    The purpose of a Seed is not simply to create activity.
                    The goal is to help create meaningful interactions,
                    encourage participation, and contribute to the
                    community's knowledge and heritage.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>

    </div>

</div>